  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves analyzing the mutagenicity of chemical compounds using data on 230 molecules tested on Salmonella typhimurium. The analysis focuses on identifying properties that influence mutagenicity, utilizing a subset of 188 molecules that are amenable to linear regression analysis, termed the \"regression friendly\" dataset. The remaining subset consists of 42 molecules which require alternative analytical approaches.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- To evaluate the mutagenic potential of chemical structures.\n- To facilitate predictive modeling using linear regression for a subset of molecules.\n- To explore database-driven methods for organizing chemical structural data.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Chemists and biologists conducting mutagenicity research.\n- Data scientists and researchers involved in chemical analysis.\n- Software developers maintaining and enhancing the database system.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Store detailed information about atoms, including their elemental type, charge, and type.\n- Manage bonds between atoms, specifying the bond type and linked atoms.\n- Store chemical compounds data with properties such as activity, logP, and LUMO values.\n- Track the active status of compounds for experimental purposes.\n- Represent ring structures within compounds, linking them with associated atoms.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- The system should ensure data integrity, maintaining consistent relationships between tables.\n- It should provide efficient querying capabilities for large datasets.\n- The database must support future scalability, accommodating additional compounds and data structures.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0117\n\nCREATE TABLE `molecule` (\n  `molecule_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `activity` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `logp` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `lumo` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `mutagenic` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`molecule_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `atom` (\n  `atom_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `molecule_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `element` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `charge` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `atom_type` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`atom_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `atom_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecule` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `bond` (\n  `bond_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `molecule_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `atom_id_1` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `atom_id_2` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `bond_type` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`bond_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `bond_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecule` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `bond_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`atom_id_1`) REFERENCES `atom` (`atom_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `bond_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`atom_id_2`) REFERENCES `atom` (`atom_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ring` (\n  `ring_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `molecule_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `ring_size` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ring_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ring_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecule` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ring_atom` (\n  `ring_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `atom_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ring_id`, `atom_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ring_atom_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`ring_id`) REFERENCES `ring` (`ring_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ring_atom_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`atom_id`) REFERENCES `atom` (`atom_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `active_compound` (\n  `active_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `molecule_id` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `is_active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n  `regression_friendly` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `notes` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`active_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `active_compound_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`molecule_id`) REFERENCES `molecule` (`molecule_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
